// Oracle question: what does a `const` with no value mean?
//
// `Const -> Ident % ST var($1,"",true,0)` (compiler.inc:47) declares it with
// an empty value string, and no document of either compiler says what that
// string becomes.  This fixture asks only whether the *declaration* is
// accepted; `const-value-read` beside it asks what reading one does.
//
// Nothing here reads LONE or FIRST, on purpose: that is the whole difference
// between the two fixtures.
//
// Register names are terminals in the original (`Arg -> A | X | Y | S`), so a
// constant may not be called `A` - which is why these are spelled out.

const LONE
const FIRST, SECOND = 7

main {
  a = SECOND
  return
}
